            <ArticleTitle>Jumper's knee.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-93</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present a clinical study on twenty six cases of a painful syndrome affecting the distal quadriceps tendon complex, popularly known as &quot;jumper's knee&quot;. They review the diagnostic aspects and discuss the treatment. In particular, they suggest a surgical approach that is not limited to the inflammatory or degenerative component of the syndrome, but also aims to correct imbalance of the extensor apparatus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
